WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.129 --> 00:00:05.300
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, thanks everyone
that submitted questions for this week’s

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.700
Arrow Flash Q&amp;A.

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:15.240
Some of you have started to ask more specific
questions about the mid season crossover episodes

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:16.560
and The CW has released a lot of information
so I’ll start off with that stuff.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:20.689
Those episodes will air December 2nd and part
2 the next day on the 3rd.

00:00:20.689 --> 00:00:24.259
So I might do something special when we get
closer to that.

00:00:24.259 --> 00:00:28.319
Question time, careful for spoilers from Arrow
and the Flash this week if you’re not caught

00:00:28.319 --> 00:00:29.319
up.

00:00:29.319 --> 00:00:33.250
Question 1 - Trek Video asks, Do you think
Harrison Wells is someone from the comics,

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:35.200
is there someone he’s trying to stop?

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:42.020
And do you think he’ll get a scene with
Oliver where he says something about his future?

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:48.710
Yes, I definitely think Harrison Wells is
someone from the comics.

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:52.850
I think Andrew Kreisberg, Geoff Johns and
Greg Berlanti and all the other people writing

00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:58.030
on the show made the smart move of doing the
comic book Rebirth story while changing some

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:04.710
of the details enough to maintain some mystery.

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:09.130
Regardless of who Harrison Wells actually
is, I think he’s a time traveler and chose

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:14.579
Harrison Wells as an homage to HG Wells as
in the classic Time Machine book.

00:01:14.579 --> 00:01:17.340
So it’s a comic book character using a fake
name.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:21.229
Here’s the people I think he could be from
most likely to least likely.

00:01:21.229 --> 00:01:26.060
And remember, he killed Simon Stagg in cold
blood, he has ice running through his veins.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:27.399
So he is not a good character.

00:01:27.399 --> 00:01:29.100
So rule any superheroes out.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:35.149
Starting with Eobard Thawne Professor Zoom,
then Impulse, Abra Kadabra and Then a version

00:01:35.149 --> 00:01:40.609
of the Rival, the original Reverse Flash.

00:01:40.609 --> 00:01:43.770
Your second question: Who or what is Harrison
Wells trying to Stop

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:48.130
I could make an hour long video talking about
how time loops and the multiverse could explain

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:49.920
why Harrison Wells is acting the way he is.

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:51.060
But short version.

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:55.270
The paper with the Crisis at the end of episode
1 is very important.

00:01:55.270 --> 00:01:57.889
It says the Barry Allen Flash disappears.

00:01:57.889 --> 00:02:01.759
I think the Reverse Flash, I’ll address
him in a sec, I think he went back in time

00:02:01.759 --> 00:02:07.149
to erase Barry Allen’s future and was successful.

00:02:07.149 --> 00:02:11.622
The timeline we’re seeing unfold on the
show is Harrison Wells going back in time

00:02:11.622 --> 00:02:14.890
to make sure Barry Allen does not disappear.

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:18.500
So Harrison Wells is guiding Barry Allen so
that he’ll be able to defeat The Reverse

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:20.460
Flash.

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:26.470
The Big Question is Why, if Harrison Wells
is evil enough to unleash Gorilla Grodd.

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:35.110
Why is 
Barry Allen someone he wants to protect?

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:40.910
I think what’s going on is Harrison Wells
is Eobard Thawne, Idolizes the Flash of the

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:45.870
past, gains the powers of the Flash but then
does something bad that leads to the creation

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:50.290
of the Hunter Zolomon Zoom and Zoom is the
one messing with the timeline.

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:59.600
So Harrison Wells still wants to cause trouble
in the future, but he’s trying to prevent

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:02.450
Hunter Zolomon from erasing both Barry Allen
and himself from the timeline.

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:06.110
If Barry Allen never became the Flash, Harrison
Wells would never become Professor Zoom in

00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:07.110
the future.

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:13.450
Sorry if that sounds confusing, you have two
Reverse Flashes, one of them is messing with

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:14.960
the timeline in a bad way.

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:18.630
The other Reverse Flash is trying to prevent
that.

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:31.630
That’s a mixture of my theories with the
other best sounding theories I’ve seen.

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:33.960
Episode 9 is called The Man in the Yellow
Suit.

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:39.080
That’s the first time Barry Allen will learn
about the Reverse Flash.

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:42.240
Here’s what I think is going on, I’ll
put this spoiler tag up even though this is

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:46.340
just a theory.

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:49.890
I think that they’re giving Harrison Wells
Professor Zoom’s storyline and they’re

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:52.430
giving Eddie Thawne Hunter Zolomon’s storyline.

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:55.770
They’re just mixing up the names to throw
people off.

00:03:55.770 --> 00:04:01.780
As for the Harrison Wells Oliver moment, yes
I definitely think it will happen.

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:04.820
When they do the first part of the Crossover
episode all of Team Arrow will go to Central

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:07.610
City and Star Labs.

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:10.720
It will be like an Arrow Cave Star Labs crossover
moment too.

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:15.150
So yes, keep your eyes peeled for Harrison
Wells dropping a Justice League easter egg.

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:18.850
Question 2 - Vince asks, who do you think
made Roy’s Suit?

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:20.299
Diggle sewing machine maybe?

00:04:20.299 --> 00:04:25.580
That’s funny, I think that he contracted
a private company to make it to his specifications.

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:27.920
I don’t think anyone on team arrow physically
made it.

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:32.630
I think Felicity probably helped design it
a little but mostly it was Oliver behind the

00:04:32.630 --> 00:04:33.630
design.

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:37.800
Remember during season 1 when Oliver is trying
to get info on Merlyn’s Dark Archer arrows

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:42.470
and Felicity tells him they’re custom made
by this really obscure private company.

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:46.850
It means that he along with Oliver probably
both order their stuff custom.

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:50.400
In Batman Begins Christian Bale had that scene
where he and Alfred talked about ordering

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:53.720
his Batman face mask and the Bat Shaped throwing
stars.

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:57.100
Just one of the benefits of being a rich super
hero or supervillain.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:00.820
You can pay people to make the crazy things
you dream up in your head.

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:04.740
Ray Palmer, Brandon Routh’s Character is
one of the few exceptions in that he has a

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:09.780
ton of money, but he also has the technical
expertise to make his own tech suit costume.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:13.630
No word on which episode that will debut but
it’s sounding like it will be the second

00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:17.840
half of the season if they just started talking
about the Black Canary costume.

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:24.010
Question 3 - Mahleks asks, do you think Cupid
Freed or Killed the guy at the end?

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:29.040
I think Cupid Killed him, in the comics she
emulates Oliver by trying to solve crimes.

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:31.090
The twist is that she kills all the criminals.

00:05:31.090 --> 00:05:34.120
That’s why she appeared at all the crime
scenes in this episode.

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:38.540
She’s following Oliver around or going to
places she knows he’ll show up.

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:42.820
Question 4 - Sam asks, what do you think the
big reveal will be in Episode 9?

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:48.070
Just to clarify episode 8 is the crossover
episode Brave and the Bold, episode 9 is the

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:49.120
mid-season finale.

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:53.590
It’s called The Climb and Alex Kingston
is guest starring again as Laurel’s mom.

00:05:53.590 --> 00:06:00.690
In terms of big WTF reveals what I’m hoping
for is Ra’s Al Ghul in Starling, a tease

00:06:00.690 --> 00:06:06.240
of the Atom and Black Canary Costumes, China
White Katana follow up and a full explanation

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:07.850
of who killed sara.

00:06:07.850 --> 00:06:09.960
Not necessarily why, just the who part.

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:14.480
That’s a lot of stuff but those are all
the biggest reveals I can think of right now.

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:18.930
Think back to the final scene from season
2 episode 9, we got the reveal of Slade being

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:22.330
the big bad in present day and the birth of
The Flash.

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:24.370
So I think we’ll see the birth of a new
superhero.

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:26.710
Either the Atom or Black Canary, maybe both.

00:06:26.710 --> 00:06:28.190
And a big villain reveal.

00:06:28.190 --> 00:06:31.660
We already know it’s Ra’s Al Ghul, so
he’ll probably do something crazy.

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:33.660
And long long shot, Sara’s Killer.

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:38.380
I don’t think this is very likely but what
if Oliver was the one who killed her and he

00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:41.080
was being controlled by someone else without
knowing it.

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:45.050
The unreliability of memory was a big theme
in this week’s episode, so Oliver could

00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:46.980
have had his mind messed with by one of the
villains.

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:52.650
That would probably be the biggest WTF reveal.

00:06:52.650 --> 00:06:57.110
Question 5 - Anshik asks, do you think we’ll
see the Lazarus Pit?

00:06:57.110 --> 00:06:59.941
Based on the way the producers have talked
about superpowers and crazy abilities I don’t

00:06:59.941 --> 00:07:00.941
think they’ll do that on Arrow.

00:07:00.941 --> 00:07:03.610
If they wanted to explain the Lazarus Pit
they’d do it on The Flash.

00:07:03.610 --> 00:07:05.550
For instance, Ray Palmer The Atom.

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:08.620
They said there aren’t any plans to make
him shrink down on Arrow.

00:07:08.620 --> 00:07:12.090
They said if they end up doing that, they’d
shrink him down on The Flash.

00:07:12.090 --> 00:07:14.320
Just because of the nature of each show.

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:17.820
Flash = Superpowers, Arrow = Crime Drama.

00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:20.510
So all the really crazy stuff will happen
on The Flash.

00:07:20.510 --> 00:07:24.639
They haven’t said they’re never going
to do Lazarus Pit, but I don’t expect it

00:07:24.639 --> 00:07:25.750
to happen this season.

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:27.639
And if they did bring anyone back, I think
it would be Tommy.

00:07:27.639 --> 00:07:29.250
But I don’t think they did that either.

00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:33.070
Question 6 - Mitzuio asks, if the Flash is
supposed to deal with Time Travel, do you

00:07:33.070 --> 00:07:38.090
think we’ll ever see a crossover with future
versions of Team Arrow or Justice League characters?

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:44.010
This season I think they’ll keep time travel
really simple and not throw in too many extra

00:07:44.010 --> 00:07:45.680
characters.

00:07:45.680 --> 00:07:49.950
I think we’ll see easter eggs for Justice
League stuff though.

00:07:49.950 --> 00:07:52.940
Like Harrison Well’s newspaper and verbal
references.

00:07:52.940 --> 00:08:05.990
But I’m not expecting to see and Old version
of Oliver or Superman or anything like that.

00:08:05.990 --> 00:08:09.270
Question 7 - J Mo asks, do you think we’ll
see Talia Al Ghul?

00:08:09.270 --> 00:08:13.720
It’s possible but DC and Warner Brothers
have this weird thing where certain characters

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:15.230
are off limits for the tv shows.

00:08:15.230 --> 00:08:16.810
Like Batman and Superman.

00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:18.860
Talia also appears in a lot of the animated
movies.

00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:21.160
So I don’t think we’ll see her this season.

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:23.850
The same thing happened with Brandon Routh’s
character.

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:29.100
Originally they’d planned for him to be
the Ted Kord Blue Beetle but Warner Brothers

00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:32.199
said they had “other plans” for that character.

00:08:32.199 --> 00:08:40.580
So they changed it and made Brandon Routh
Ray Palmer instead.

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:50.050
Thanks so much everyone for submitting questions,
I think that covers most of the important

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:51.050
stuff.

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:56.810
Here’s some more details on the Crossover
Episodes.

00:08:56.810 --> 00:09:02.680
Captain Boomerang will be the reason Team
Arrow goes to Central City and vice versa.

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:07.740
And the reason the first episode is called
Flash versus Arrow is because of a meta human

00:09:07.740 --> 00:09:10.840
messing with Barry Allen’s mind.

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:14.660
It’s supposed to be Rainbow Raider or Chroma,
how ever you want to think of him.

00:09:14.660 --> 00:09:18.580
Like I said, I’ll try to do some extra special
stuff when that all goes down so be sure to

00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:23.430
subscribe to get everything and follow me
on twitter and facebook for updates.

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:27.620
Links for all that stuff in the description.

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:34.170
Next week Cupid versus Arrow, so click here
to catch up on this week’s episode and click

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:35.490
here for this week’s flash episode.

00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:37.910
Thanks for watching, boxing glove arrow to
the face, boom.

